//! The `ui/*` routes of the Files tab and the File tab, listed by the host (`host.rs` registers them with the
//! others): `(name, description)`. The UI registers the matching handlers: `files` and `editors` with the File tab
//! (`ui/src/features/files/register.tsx`), `explorer` with the Git browser (`ui/src/features/git-browser/register.tsx`).
//! Moved out of `host.rs` in when `editors` and `explorer` were added (size limit). The Debug API coverage
//! check reads the route names from this file, `host.rs` and `terminal.rs`.
//!
//! Depends on: nothing. Called by: `host.rs`.

/// `files` (the shown document and its editor), `editors` (the editor workspace: tabs, the pair, compare,
/// the close dialog) and `explorer` (the Files tab: folders, History, search, the folder actions).
pub(crate) const FILES_ROUTES: &[(&str, &str)] = &[
    (
        "editors",
        "The editor workspace beside the chat (file tabs, the +N open-files list, two editors side by side, compare with the saved version, the unsaved-changes dialog, folding chat and sessions), every action its controls and keys have. Body: {action: state|activate|openToSide|restore|focus|ratio|fold|compareSaved|closeSavedVersion|close|closeDialog|closeSavedTabs|chat|sessions|swap|openFilesIn, sessionId?, ...}: state (default) = the open files as tabs and the +N list show them (file, name, display, saved, unsaved, changed, mark, visible, active), hidden (+N), the pair (left, right, focus, compare), ratio, folded, problem (why a compare is not offered), closeDialog (file, title, problem) and the chat/sessions slot layout; activate {file} = a tab click or a +N row; openToSide {file?} = the split button (Ctrl \\); restore; focus {side: left|right}; ratio {ratio: 0.25..0.75}; fold {side, folded?}; compareSaved = Compare with saved version (the last commit, read-only on the left); closeSavedVersion; close {file?} = the tab's X or Ctrl W (an unsaved file opens the dialog); closeDialog {choice: cancel|discard|save} (save never overwrites a file changed on disk: the dialog stays with its problem); closeSavedTabs; chat {folded}; sessions {folded}; swap = Ctrl B; openFilesIn {mode: tabs|single}. The shown file's text and editor are ui/files.",
    ),
    (
        "files",
        "The File tab (files the agent mentions, previewed, and its editor) of a session, every action a click has (the Debug API acts as the user, no native dialogs). Body: {action: state|refs|open|ref-menu|switch|close|reload|mode|external|edit|openEdit|setText|saveEdit|cancelEdit|reloadEdit|keepEditing|compare|drop, sessionId?: string (default: the selected session), ...}: state = the shown file (name, path relative to the session folder), kind, size, status, mode, truncation, the text it shows (up to 65,536 characters), editNotice (why the editor did not open), the viewer, the recent list, the last drop report and editor (null when closed, else {text, textCut, dirty, conflict, problem, saving, compare, wrap, baselineFingerprint, diskFingerprint}); refs {entryId?} = the file references the transcript shows (text, path, line, state ok|no|pending; an ambiguous name carries its choices); open {text, line?} resolves a path as the transcript does (the window's scope: the session folder and picked folders), or open {file} a handle from refs or the recent list; ref-menu {text, item?: open|edit|reveal|copy-path, file?, line?} is a linked name's right-click menu: without item it answers the items and canEdit, or {choices: [{file, display, kind, size}], total} for an ambiguous name (at most 50; act on one by giving its file handle with the item; nothing ambiguous opens by itself); edit opens the editor (pictures and binary files have none), reveal shows the file in its folder, copy-path copies the path the tab shows; switch {file}; close; reload; mode {mode: rendered|source}; external {what: open|reveal} opens with the default app or shows in the folder (a program is never opened); drop {files: [{name, data (base64), folder?}]} routes files like a drop on the composer and answers the drop report and the composer's pictures, context chips and document chips. Known secrets in a file's text are hidden like in every answer (see the top of this page). edit {text} saves the shown text file with that whole text like the editor's Save: refused with `stale` when the file changed on disk since the tab read it; line endings and a byte-order mark are kept; the agent gets a context chip with the diff. The editor, like the window's: openEdit opens the shown complete text file in it (nothing is saved); setText {text} replaces the editor's text (LF line endings; an empty string is allowed); saveEdit answers outcome saved|unchanged|stale (a stale save keeps the draft and shows the conflict, it never overwrites the newer file on disk; the file's line endings and byte-order mark are kept); cancelEdit drops the draft; reloadEdit drops the draft and reads the file again; keepEditing hides the conflict banner; compare opens a read-only Mine/Disk comparison.",
    ),
    (
        "explorer",
        "The Files tab (folders, History, search), every action its controls have; acting shows the tab first. Body: {action: state|place|view|expand|collapse|more|changedOnly|showIgnored|refresh|search|openFirst|open|historyMore|version|back|pending|reviewSession|review|closeReview|commit|askRevert|cancelRevert|confirmRevert|enableHistory|identity|cancelHistory|confirmHistory, ...}: state (default) = the folder, Places, view, summary (branch, changed, commits), tree rows (path, directory, depth, expanded, changed, more), search results (names, hits with line, commits), History (commits, more, the changes since the last commit), an open commit's files and the folder actions; place {folder} (one of Places); view {view: files|history}; expand/collapse {path}; more {path?} (next page); changedOnly/showIgnored {on}; search {query} answers with the results; openFirst = Enter; open {path, line?} opens the File tab (never starts a session); historyMore; version {id}; back; pending {open}. Before a session: review, closeReview, commit (the Commit dialog: finish it with ui/git and sessionId = commitKey), askRevert then confirmRevert or cancelRevert (the core rechecks head, fingerprint and new files), enableHistory then identity {name, email} and confirmHistory or cancelHistory. In a session reviewSession opens the Changes tab.",
    ),
];
